{
 "duration": 74,
 "lines": [
  [
   0.3,
   5.4,
   "Weft's new thread screen lets you quickly start a new thread, and control how it runs."
  ],
  [
   5.7,
   11.28,
   "This video is playing in your browser pane. Most of Weft's replies will show you something here."
  ],
  [
   11.98,
   21.23,
   "Some tips. First, tell your AI what to build: type it, paste screenshots, or hit the mic and just talk. Option apostrophe starts and stops the mic."
  ],
  [
   21.93,
   30.98,
   "When you have a big idea, use the mic, and talk, and talk, and talk. Get all your ideas out in one big wall of text, and let your AI sort it out."
  ],
  [
   31.68,
   38.23,
   "For small ideas, give Weft simple instructions. You'll be surprised how well your AI can improvise."
  ],
  [
   38.93,
   46.65,
   "Speaking of improvising: when you don't know exactly how to do something, ask your AI. It will show you a plan in the browser pane."
  ],
  [
   47.35,
   60.2,
   "Try not to work on the same screen or product area in more than one thread at once, so you avoid conflicts. Weft has smart, built-in conflict resolution, but if you know you're going to hit a conflict, use worktrees."
  ],
  [
   60.9,
   67.5,
   "For bigger tasks, tell your AI to use subagents, so it can fan out and work through the plan in parallel."
  ],
  [
   68.2,
   72.5,
   "Now let's get to work. What do you want to build today?"
  ]
 ],
